 "answerVoice": "female",
 "notes": "Three women: one in flowery leggings (main), two dressed all in black (one in a short top with a white waistband, one in a T-shirt). The two in black are hard to tell apart, so only the short-top woman is a target and only where she is clear: standing left of the other at 0.0, crouching and sliding in head first 3.0-4.0, lying behind the main woman 4.5-5.5; off afterwards (6.5-7.0 the jumper is the T-shirt woman). At 5.0 and 5.5 the two bodies overlap: the main woman's box holds head and upper body only, her legs on the right are unboxed. From 7.5 the face on the left with the watch is taken to be the main woman (her leggings join it); the half-hidden second face is not boxed. 'to cover her eyes' is at 2.5 s. Still 2.0: 'a woman' and 'trousers' label the same figure, 0.38 apart in x."
